// There is a TCP stack and a UDP stack, and there is no socket table joining
// a descriptor to a connection in either — sys_socket below hands out no
// descriptor to join. So these four have nothing to send on and nothing to
// receive from.
//
// send returning `len` was the worst of the twenty: a program that sent a
// buffer was told every byte went out. recv returning 0 was read as a closed
// connection, so a reader stopped rather than hung — the same wrong answer,
// quieter.
fn sys_send(sockfd: u32, buf: u64, len: u64, flags: u32): u64 {
  if buf == 0 { return EINVAL }
